<!--
stele.md: this project's rules for coding agents (created by stele init {{.Version}}).
stele reads this file and never edits it. You may delete this comment.

Rules are separated by a line holding only ---. A rule may start with
key: value lines, then a blank line, then the rule in plain prose:

  scope: ["**/*.go"]
  check: regex
  pattern: fmt\.Print
  blocking: false

  Log through the shared logger, never fmt.Print.

scope     path globs. Before the agent writes a matching file, it is shown
          the rule. A rule with no scope is shown for every file: keep few.
check     regex: stele checks each write, and stele check in CI, for pattern.
pattern   the regex for check: regex (Go RE2), taken as written: quotes
          are part of it.
message   what a violation says; the start of the rule by default.
blocking  true (the default with check) or false: whether a violation
          blocks the agent and fails stele check.
-->
